+# DeepEye four-channel sample-scan capture candidate
+
+Status: author candidate under DEEPEYE-IMPLEMENTATION-20261014/v1. Product
+decisions, independent acceptance and publication remain with the registered
+product main. This document does not claim a public ABI, board result or
+physical acquisition authority.
+
+## Scope
+
+`deepeye_sample_scan_capture.sv` is a one-clock event collector for four input
+positions numbered 0 through 3. The positions are not physical pins, ADC
+channels or calibrated sources. `sample_data` is a 16-bit container and does
+not assert 16-bit ADC precision. `sample_tick` and `sample_quality` are opaque
+transport values: zero, repeated, decreasing or wrapped values are preserved
+without interpretation. The local event ordinal is not the public ABI
+`sample_id`.
+
+The module has no input ready. Every asserted `sample_strobe` at an armed
+ordinary clock edge is one observed event. Output backpressure cannot stop
+front-end observation or ordinals. There is no missing-strobe timeout.
+
+## Parameters and interface
+
+| Parameter | Default | Supported |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| `SEQ_W` | 32 | 2..32 |
+| `TICK_W` | 64 | 1..64 |
+| `TAG_W` | 32 | 1..64 |
+| `STAT_W` | 32 | 2..32 |
+
+Inputs: `clk`, `rst`, `stop`, `rearm`, `rearm_tag[TAG_W-1:0]`,
+`sample_strobe`, `sample_channel[1:0]`, `sample_data[15:0]`,
+`sample_tick[TICK_W-1:0]`, `sample_quality[7:0]`, `out_ready`.
+
+Outputs: `out_valid`, `out_data[63:0]`,
+`out_ticks[4*TICK_W-1:0]`, `out_quality[31:0]`,
+`out_first_seq[SEQ_W-1:0]`, `out_last_seq[SEQ_W-1:0]`,
+`out_tag[TAG_W-1:0]`, `armed`, `partial_len[2:0]`,
+`next_seq[SEQ_W-1:0]`, `seq_exhausted`, `order_error_event`,
+`overrun_event`, `seq_exhaust_event`, and six `STAT_W`-bit counters.
+
+Channel 0 occupies the least-significant lane of every packed output.
+`out_valid` says only that one complete record is available for transport. It
+does not certify fresh, live or physically valid acquisition. Inactive output
+payload is unspecified.
+
+## Parameter legality
+
+Port declarations use legal clamped effective widths so an illegal parameter
+can compile and reach the actual module guard instead of failing on a negative
+range. The effective widths are bounded ternaries over `SEQ_W`, `TICK_W`,
+`TAG_W` and `STAT_W`. Under `ifndef SYNTHESIS`, the module emits exactly one of:
+
+```text
+deepeye_sample_scan_capture: SEQ_W out of range
+deepeye_sample_scan_capture: TICK_W out of range
+deepeye_sample_scan_capture: TAG_W out of range
+deepeye_sample_scan_capture: STAT_W out of range
+```
+
+Each invalid case was compiled and reached an exact `$fatal(1, "...")` from
+this module with no compiler warning. Synthesis exclusion is intentional;
+out-of-range parameters are not a supported synthesized configuration.
+
+## Abort and window rules
+
+Priority is `rst > stop > rearm > ordinary edge`. Any asserted abort input
+combinations immediately qualifies `out_valid` low and inhibits sample intake
+and output retirement on that edge. Reset and stop clear partial state, the
+complete slot, tag, ordinals, event pulses and counters and leave `armed=0`.
+Rearm performs the same clear, stores exactly `rearm_tag`, sets `next_seq=0`
+and `armed=1`. Same-tag rearm is legal and flushes every old record and partial.
+
+## Scan assembly
+
+A valid scan is four consecutive observed events with channels 0,1,2,3 in
+that exact order. The first event captures its ordinal; a completed record's
+`out_last_seq` is exactly `out_first_seq + 3`. Each lane preserves the event's
+data, raw tick and raw quality.
+
+At empty partial state, channel 0 starts a scan. Channels 1 through 3 are
+orphan events: one order-error pulse, one order-error count and one discarded
+sample. From partial length 1 through 3, only the matching channel extends the
+scan; length 3 matching channel 3 completes it. A wrong channel causes one
+order error and discards the previously collected prefix. If that wrong
+channel is 0, it simultaneously starts a new prefix. Otherwise the current
+event is lost too. A terminal event is processed through these order rules
+before namespace exhaustion is applied, so a terminal new prefix is discarded
+and counted once.
+
+`SEQ_W=2` supplies four events, ordinals 0..3, exactly one complete window.
+The event at `2**SEQ_W-1` is processed, then `armed` clears, `seq_exhausted`
+becomes sticky, `next_seq` holds the maximum ordinal and no further event is
+accepted until explicit rearm. A partial at exhaustion is discarded in full.
+An already complete output record remains transportable.
+
+## Output slot and accounting
+
+There is one complete-result slot in addition to the bounded partial. A new
+completion is registered into the slot and cannot be retired on its completion
+edge. If the old slot is full and retiring, the old record retires and the new
+record refills atomically. If it is full and not retiring, the new complete
+scan is dropped, the old payload remains stable, one overrun pulse is emitted,
+and four samples plus one overrun are counted. Order checking and ordinals
+continue under backpressure.
+
+All six counters saturate at `2**STAT_W-1`; additions are widened before
+saturation and saturation cannot affect data flow. Within a window and before
+saturation:
+
+```text
+stat_events = 4 * (stat_retired + occupied_complete_slot)
+            + partial_len + stat_discarded_samples
+stat_scans  = stat_retired + occupied_complete_slot + stat_overruns
+```
+
+Slot occupancy is internal state; `out_valid` is additionally abort-qualified.
+Counters do not accumulate across reset, stop or rearm boundaries.
+
